// src/v4/extdeps/languages/cpp.dag
//
// Scope: C++ language model — direction-agnostic. Subsumes C subset (C is a syntactic subset of C++).
// Anchor: https://www.iso.org/standard/79358.html (ISO/IEC 14882, C++ standard) + https://en.cppreference.com
// Unifies: (per THESIS:188) language spec = transport spec = interpreter runtime. ONE substrate carrier for all three roles. Different lenses read different facts from the same data (emission reads syntax; transport reads serialization; interpreter reads execution semantics). A worker needing transport or runtime extends this file, not a new "transport spec" file.
//
// Owns:
//   - C++ grammar (declarations, expressions, statements, templates, classes)
//   - Type system (primitive types + struct + union + class + template instantiation)
//   - Inhabitance: int -> OrderedRing, std::string -> FreeMonoid<char>, std::vector<T> -> ...
//   - Cost realization: per-operation cost on C++ targets
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/algebra.dag, std/primitive.dag
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-4
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.extdeps.languages.cpp

